    {
      "id": "govweb",
      "title": "Nepal .gov.np web-infrastructure observations",
      "status": "experimental",
      "description": "Passive observations of Nepal's public-sector web infrastructure: the canonical local-level roster, the Certificate Transparency hostname inventory, an evidence-bearing hostname-to-local-level attribution, and per-hostname hosting, DNS, TLS and HTTP behaviour. The unit of record is a hostname, not a local level, because a hostname can belong to an office the roster does not contain; attribution to a local level is a separate join whose method and evidence URL are recorded on every row. Collection uses ordinary public requests only and never scans ports, probes for vulnerabilities, or bypasses robots.txt.",
      "grain": "one row per hostname per observation (hosting, DNS, TLS, HTTP headers, robots, scripts, reachability); the roster table is one row per local level, the attribution table one row per level-to-hostname link (an unresolved level appears once with an empty hostname; 47 levels carry a second alias hostname), the entities table one row per apex hostname, the entity_hosting table one row per apex joining owner type to addresses, RDAP operators and reachability, and the sites table one row per discovered hostname",
      "coverage": {
        "start": "2026-11-05",
        "end": "2026-11-09",
        "note": "Hostname discovery and per-host observations are a 2026-11-05 snapshot over a 20-hostname pilot sample; attribution, the roster adjudication and manual overrides were extended through 2026-11-09 across all 753 local levels over the 2,837-hostname discovered inventory. The pilot sample is not a census of the discovered hostnames."
      },
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "Office of the Auditor General — local-level report API",
          "url": "https://oag.gov.np/api/front/local-level-report?province=&district=&municipality=&fiscal_year=&page=1&per_page=2000"
        },
        {
          "name": "Certificate Transparency search (crt.sh)",
          "url": "https://crt.sh/?q=%25.gov.np&output=json"
        },
        {
          "name": "Local-body e-office directory (dcc-localbody-list)",
          "url": "http://eoffice.mahalaxmimun.gov.np/dcc-localbody-list"
        },
        {
          "name": "Wikidata Query Service — P856 official website",
          "url": "https://query.wikidata.org/sparql"
        },
        {
          "name": "OpenStreetMap Overpass API — Nepal administrative relations",
          "url": "https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter"
        },
        {
          "name": "IP registration metadata (ipwho.is)",
          "url": "https://ipwho.is/"
        },
        {
          "name": "Cloudflare DNS-over-HTTPS resolver",
          "url": "https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query"
        }
      ],
      "verification": {
        "status": "partial",
        "method": "roster reconciled against the official 753 local levels after adjudicating 12 extra records; every active local level is either attributed or explicitly unresolved; attributed hostnames are unique, end in .gov.np, and appear in a committed discovery source; manual rejections stay unlinked and acceptances stay applied; every mapped row carries method, evidence URL and decision date; every discovered apex hostname carries an entity classification, unknown-typed rows carry no guessed method, and local-level entity ids reconcile with the attribution; every entity_hosting row joins to an entity and a reachability state; observation hostnames are checked against the discovery inventory",
        "report": "reconciliation.json"
      },
      "pipeline": {
        "package": "govweb",
        "cli": [
          "python -m govweb.cli roster",
          "python -m govweb.cli discover-ct",
          "python -m govweb.cli attribute",
          "python -m govweb.cli entities",
          "python -m govweb.cli reachability",
          "python -m govweb.cli rdap",
          "python -m govweb.cli globalping kathmandu.gov.np aadarshakotwalmun.gov.np --locations NP IN DE",
          "python -m govweb.cli sample",
          "python -m govweb.cli collect",
          "python -m govweb.cli report",
          "python -m govweb.cli build",
          "python -m govweb.cli verify"
        ],
        "plan": "docs/plans/govweb-audit.md"
      },
      "license": {
        "code": "MIT",
        "data": "MIT; derived from public government and Certificate Transparency responses, attribution required"
      },
      "tags": [
        "digital-infrastructure",
        "local-government",
        "hosting",
        "dns",
        "tls",
        "http-headers",
        "attribution",
        "entity-classification",
        "nepal"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The 20-hostname observation sample is a deterministic lexicographic pilot, not a census of the 2,837 discovered hostnames or the 753 local levels.",
        "Attribution is not proof of administrative ownership: it records the best available source agreement, with the method and evidence URL on every row.",
        "The local-body directory contains duplicate rows and some wrong or generic links; a row is accepted only when its hostname is a plausible .gov.np local-level name and is not already owned by another local level.",
        "Unresolved local levels are evidence of missing data, not evidence that the local level has no website.",
        "Manual corrections are recorded in attribution_overrides.json so a reviewer can see every deviation from the automatic result.",
        "Non-local government agencies and province portals are not attributed to a local level even when their names collide.",
        "A failed or missing observation is never treated as a secure configuration.",
        "Country-level IP geolocation is approximate and does not establish the physical server location or the hosting contract.",
        "robots.txt directives are publisher instructions, not access control; robots-disallowed hostnames retain no script data."
      ],
